media: h713-hdmirx: derive the ring geometry from the rowbyte and INCAP active

The V4L2 format has to describe the RING the firmware writes, not the
SOURCE it receives. The two coincide on the HY310 (1920x1080 panel) and
differ on a board whose panel is smaller than the source: the firmware scales
inside its capture path, and the ring then holds fewer pixels than the source
sends. Measured on the HY300 Pro (1280x720 panel) with a 1920x1080 source,
19.09.2026: INCAP active (+0x874) 0x07800438 = 1920x1080, INCAP rowbyte
(+0x924) 0x00360036 = 54 * 16 = 864 bytes per NV16 luma line. 864 bytes of
luma are 864 pixels, not 1920. Until now G_FMT answered the source size with
the ring's pitch - an inconsistent format (owner dmesg, test 5: "INCAP-
Zeilenabstand 0x00500050 passt nicht zur Breite 1920") - and h713-tv refused
the plane against the panel on the source's size (issue #1).

The rule, with the rowbyte as the only primary source
(h713_hdmirx_ring_geometry()):

  pitch = rowbyte * 16 (a rowbyte of zero or unequal luma/chroma halves keep
  the ALIGN(width, 16) fallback with its line).
  pitch >= ALIGN(active width, 16): the firmware does not scale, the ring is
  INCAP active - every HY310 case, byte-identical to today's format.
  pitch < ALIGN(active width, 16): the firmware scales; ring width = pitch
  (the tightest width a pitch admits), ring height = active height * pitch /
  active width, rounded down to an even line count (479.25 measured as 478;
  the plane refuses odd heights). 864 x 486 for the case above.
  Cross-check, optional: the DE picture scaler's input window (+0x34 of
  syscon@5180000, allwinner,scaler) names the ring exactly, 852x478 here. It
  is taken only after the rowbyte said the firmware scales, only when
  ALIGN(its width, 16) == pitch and its height is within two lines of the
  source's aspect ratio applied to that width, and never on a board where
  the rowbyte says the ring is the source. Without the phandle the
  arithmetic stands.

Why the scaler window may never be primary (K3 v1, dev17, HY310,
20.09.2026): the firmware writes it only when it rebuilds its window chain -
the first lock of a boot and every republished descriptor - not on every
source change. After 720p -> 1080p it still read 1280x720 while INCAP and
the rowbyte had moved to 1920x1080 / 0x78; taken as the ring it produced a
1280x720 format with a 1920-byte pitch: a sheared picture, then the console,
not recoverable by replugging. Under this rule that state gives 1920x1080 /
1920 because the rowbyte equals the aligned width; the window is not even
read.

Two more things that kept h713-tv's status on "change in flight" over a
picture that was up and right:

  - The record the firmware writes after OUR descriptor republish (VideoDec,
    30.00 Hz, color_format 0) echoes the descriptor's frame size, which is
    the ring h713-tv put on the plane - not the source. Compared against
    INCAP active it says "change in flight" for as long as the picture
    stands whenever ring != source (852x478 against 1920x1080). It is now
    recognised before that comparison and takes no part in it; a genuine
    HDMI record is compared as before.
  - A direct release after a republish ends without any word from the
    firmware. A client that asked during the release was told -ENOLCK and
    may have stopped asking (h713-tv gives up after 2 s; a release can take
    longer). The release now ends with a source change event so that it
    looks again.

G_FMT reports ring width x ring height with bytesperline = pitch; the plane
size, the queue and the debugfs "format:" line use the same numbers; the
timing (QUERY/G_DV_TIMINGS) stays the source. One ratelimited line when the
ring is not the source, none when it is: "source 1920x1080, ring 852x478
pitch 864 - the firmware scales (by the picture scaler)".

Host model over the five measured cases in umbau/work/K3v2/model (cases 1-3
byte-identical to today's driver). Follow-up to 0136e, which stays
byte-identical; 0136g adds the optional syscon node.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

